{# DEPARTMENTS — the org chart's home.

   DESIGN PROVENANCE, STATED BECAUSE IT IS MIXED. The team-module design set
   draws no standalone departments page: its folder tree is the roster, the
   member record, the invite flow, the permission matrix and the three document
   rungs, and a departments screen is not among them. So this page is composed
   from vocabulary that IS drawn, and every borrowing is named here so the
   composition can be ruled on retroactively rather than discovered later:

     · THE PAGE HEAD — title, the org-wide sentence, and the one-field create
       form in the actions slot — is the old application's `/departments` page
       (DesignsProjects/uhifadhi-web/departments/index.html), adapted. What is
       NOT taken from it is everything belonging to the retired world in which a
       department was a module lens with its own dashboard: no widget surface,
       no performance board, no per-department page. A department grants
       nothing and now owns nothing but positions.

     · THE BODY is the positions design set's direction C, "a card per
       department" — `.dcard`, `.dhead`, `.dmeta`, `.plist`, `.pitem`. That
       vocabulary already ships in public/team.css, ported with the matrix and
       until now unused by any template, because the matrix put direction C on
       the platform's plate instead. It is used here for the reason it was drawn:
       two departments may own the same word, and in separate cards they can
       never be read as one job.

     · THE UNASSIGNED CARD and its sentence are the roster's org-chart band,
       which already ships and already had to explain that Unassigned is not a
       department.

     · THE RENAME CONTROL is the one the permission matrix's pane header ships:
       a compact field the button submits, because the route needs a name and a
       bare `Rename` button has nowhere to collect one.

   NOT A WIDGET SURFACE. No directions were drawn for this screen and the
   standing rule is that a direction ships because it was drawn — six invented
   renderings would be a design made by the implementation.

   NO KPI STRIP. The workspace rule puts KPI cards at the top of a page that has
   them; nothing draws KPIs for departments, so there are none. #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiShell/page.html.twig' %}
{% import '@UhifadhiTeam/positions/_bits.html.twig' as pm %}

{% block title %}Departments{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@UhifadhiTeam/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_tabs %}{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}
    <a href="{{ path('team_index') }}">uhifadhi</a> / departments
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Departments{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}
    A <b>department</b> is a part of the organisation that owns positions &mdash; Ecology, Protection Service,
    Administration. It is <b>org-wide</b>, like the team itself: made once here, and read by every area and every
    module that groups by it. A position&rsquo;s name is unique only inside its department, which is why
    <span class="mono">Ecology / Analyst</span> and <span class="mono">Protection Service / Analyst</span> are two
    different jobs rather than a clash. <b>A department grants nothing</b>: filing a position here changes where
    it is read and never what anybody may do &mdash; capability arrives through that position&rsquo;s permissions,
    which live on <a href="{{ path('team_positions') }}">the matrix</a>.
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_actions %}
    {# ONE FIELD, SO IT IS ONE FIELD — not a screen. Straight from the old
       application's departments page, which got this right. #}
    <form class="assign" method="post" action="{{ path('team_department_create') }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
        <input type="text" name="name" class="fld" placeholder="New department" aria-label="New department name" required>
        <button class="cta" type="submit">{{ pm.icon_plus() }} Add</button>
    </form>
    <a class="tgl" href="{{ path('team_positions') }}">{{ pm.icon_people() }} Positions &amp; permissions</a>
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
    <div data-dp>
        {% if departments is empty %}
            {# THE STATE THAT MADE THIS SCREEN NECESSARY, and the one a fresh
               installation is in: the roster bands by a department nothing can
               create, so every position reads Unassigned forever. The control
               that ends it is the field in the page header, and this says so
               rather than leaving an empty page to be interpreted. #}
            <div class="pm-first">
                {{ pm.icon_plus() }}
                <div class="ft">
                    <h3>There are no departments yet, and the field above is what makes the first one.</h3>
                    <p>Until one exists, every position on this installation belongs to nobody in particular:
                    the roster&rsquo;s org chart bands them all as <b>Unassigned</b> and the permission matrix
                    groups them under <b>No department yet</b>. Neither is a fault and nothing is broken by it
                    &mdash; a department is an organizational fact, so an installation that has not decided on
                    one yet is simply an installation that has not decided.</p>
                    <p>Three or four is usually the whole list. Type the first one above.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="tm-cardgrid">
            {% for department in departments %}
                {% set positions = owned[department.uuidString]|default([]) %}
                {% set people = headcount[department.uuidString]|default(0) %}
                <div class="dcard">
                    <div class="dhead">
                        <div class="dh-l">
                            <i class="dot"></i>
                            <b>{{ department.name }}</b>
                        </div>
                        <div class="dh-r">
                            {# THE RENAME FIELD THE BUTTON SUBMITS — the matrix's
                               pane header ships exactly this, for the same
                               reason: the route needs a name and a bare button
                               has nowhere to collect one. #}
                            <form class="assign" method="post" action="{{ path('team_department_rename', {uuid: department.uuidString}) }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                                <input type="text" name="name" class="fld pm-rename" value="{{ department.name }}"
                                       aria-label="Rename {{ department.name }}" required>
                                <button class="softbtn" type="submit">Rename</button>
                            </form>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="dmeta">
                        {{ positions|length }} position{{ positions|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot;
                        {{ people }} {{ people == 1 ? 'person' : 'people' }}
                    </div>

                    {% if positions|length %}
                        <div class="plist">
                            {% for position in positions %}
                                {{ include('@UhifadhiTeam/departments/_position.html.twig', {
                                    position: position,
                                    departments: departments,
                                    here: department,
                                    holders: holders,
                                    csrfToken: csrfToken,
                                }, with_context: false) }}
                            {% endfor %}
                        </div>
                    {% else %}
                        <p class="dnote">No positions are filed here yet. Move one in from another card, or make
                        one on the matrix &mdash; a department with none is a heading waiting for its first job.</p>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            {% endfor %}

            {# THE LOOSE POSITIONS. Dashed, because it is not a department and
               the page has to say so in words — a reader meeting it for the
               first time will otherwise read it as a department called "No
               department yet". The roster's org chart already carries this
               sentence for the same reason. #}
            {% if loose|length %}
                <div class="dcard un">
                    <div class="dhead">
                        <div class="dh-l">
                            <i class="dot un"></i>
                            <b>No department yet</b>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <p class="dnote">This is <b>not a department</b> &mdash; it is every position nobody has filed
                    yet. A position may be created before anybody has decided which part of the organisation owns
                    it, and its holders read as <b>Unassigned</b> on the roster until one is chosen here.</p>

                    <div class="dmeta">
                        {{ loose|length }} position{{ loose|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot;
                        {{ looseHeadcount }} {{ looseHeadcount == 1 ? 'person' : 'people' }}
                    </div>

                    <div class="plist">
                        {% for position in loose %}
                            {{ include('@UhifadhiTeam/departments/_position.html.twig', {
                                position: position,
                                departments: departments,
                                here: null,
                                holders: holders,
                                csrfToken: csrfToken,
                            }, with_context: false) }}
                        {% endfor %}
                    </div>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
